</div></section>

<section><p class="page-kicker">Connection modes</p><h2>Bluetooth and 2.4 GHz are not the same connection.</h2>
<p>Before you start flashing firmware, check the switch on the side of the V6 Max. Bluetooth and the 2.4 GHz receiver use different pairing methods. For Bluetooth, choose BT mode and hold <strong>Fn + 1</strong> (or 2/3) for roughly <strong>4–6 seconds</strong>. Its 2.4 GHz receiver procedure is different: set 2.4G mode, hold <strong>Fn + 4</strong> for four seconds, then insert the receiver.</p>
<div class="article-cards">
<div><strong>Bluetooth fails, wired USB works</strong><p>Keyboard power and the basic key matrix are working. Focus on BT mode, saved host record, selected profile and another Bluetooth host.</p></div>
<div><strong>Bluetooth fails, 2.4 GHz works</strong><p>Test another Bluetooth profile and a second host before treating the whole keyboard as defective.</p></div>
<div><strong>2.4 GHz receiver fails</strong><p>Recheck the dedicated receiver pairing process and a different USB port. A Bluetooth pairing reset does not pair the receiver.</p></div>
<div><strong>Neither wireless mode works</strong><p>Fully charge the board, review current Keychron troubleshooting, and contact support with firmware information before attempting a flash.</p></div>
</div>
<h2>How to document the fault for Keychron support</h2>
<p>Record the board's exact V6 Max variant and keyboard layout, the side-switch mode, the profile or receiver procedure used, whether the keys flashed, and whether a second host detected it. Keychron specifically requests connection behavior and firmware version evidence in its current support article.</p>
<p><strong>Firmware risk:</strong> Keychron maintains separate keyboard, Bluetooth and receiver firmware paths. Use the vendor's instructions only for the exact hardware version and only when its troubleshooting indicates an update is necessary. A wrong image can cause a more serious problem than an old pairing record.</p>
<p class="meta">Source: <a href="https://help-center.keychron.com/en-us/article/35953445831575-troubleshooting-keychron-v-max-q-max-k-max-wireless-connection-issues">Keychron official V Max wireless troubleshooting, updated August 2026</a>. Not a claim of a new physical keyboard test.</p></section>

